    sections: [
      {
        type: 'about',
        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Vira',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Vira is Sweden's historic national card game (19th century). 3-4 players (3 active). 52-card deck. 13 each + 13-card talon. Complex bidding with ~40 contract types. KÃ¶pspel (buy from talon), Solospel (no talon), Gaskspel (take all talon). Declarer vs 2 defenders. Scoring via 'virapulla' (token pot).",
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: "Vira is Sweden's national card game and the most elaborate of the Solo family (with Solo Whist and Préférence). Tradition holds it was invented around 1810 at Vira courthouse when a storm snowbound the court; two Walloon gentlemen are said to have devised it. It was the most advanced and popular card game in Sweden for a long time; popularity declined after Contract Bridge arrived in the early 1930s because Vira never became standardized like Skat.",
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '3-4 (if 4, dealer sits out)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '52 cards. 13 each. 13-card talon (stock).',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards, virapulla (scoring pot with tokens)',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: '13 each, 13 to talon.',
              },
            ],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
